caveats:
  - "Section attribution is weak: the table of contents lost its section-number column in PDF extraction, so headings are recognized by shape alone and most clauses attribute to a distant ancestor heading. Records affected carry needs_human_review with the line distance."
  - "Requirement detection is keyword-based over normalized paragraphs. A requirement whose keyword was hyphenated or shredded across a table cell is missed and is NOT counted as extracted."
  - "Register field rows are recovered by ordinal pairing of column runs and are emitted only when all four runs agree in length. Tables that disagree emit a review record and NO field rows."
  - "A 'parsed' table means its column runs agreed, NOT that every field of that register was recovered. A register figure continued across a page break is split by the intervening caption, so the rows emitted for any one register are a LOWER BOUND: CAP yielded 2 rows for a register that has far more fields. Field rows are trustworthy individually; the per-register field set is incomplete."
  - "register_tables_attempted counts every caption of the shape 'Figure N: Offset ...', which includes table-of-contents caption rows and page-break continuations, so the attempted denominator is inflated relative to the number of distinct registers."
